<title>CHINA: INDIA'S TATA ELECTRIC LAUNCHES US$300 MLN IN BONDS.</title>
<headline>INDIA'S TATA ELECTRIC LAUNCHES US$300 MLN IN BONDS.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's Tata Electric Companies have launched a two-tranche US$300 million 144a bond issue, lead manager Chase Manhattan said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The US$150 million bond due August 2007 pays a semi-annual coupon of 7-7/8 percent and was priced at 99.611 to yield 7.93 percent or 160 basis points over 10-year U.S. Treasuries.</p>
<p>The US$150 million bond due August 2017 pays a semi-annual coupon of 8-1/2 percent and was priced at 99.354 to yield 8.568 percent or 193 basis points over the 6-5/8 percent Treasury bond due 2027.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong News Room (852) 2843 6371</p>
